      "text": "/skill:tidy-recipe-authoring\n\nCreate tidy recipes for workbook `bd379bac8249bfb46e6befdb0a2fdbf088c7ea6cc8665c7c925b0385c1098916--45100do013_2010.xlsx`.\n\n- Publication: Recorded Crime — Victims (Australian Bureau of Statistics)\n- Release or year: 2010\n- Sheets needing a recipe: 5 of 5\n\n| sheet | sheet_sha256 | current recipe |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Contents\" | 92e2d0f582cb96c819950e34502b195281265f0bba8fcfe9b80724e446afb608 | missing |\n| \"Table_1\" | 42a838aeb8877c9605024d9653e39d95738a501287c2efc68a1f4f915b747413 | missing |\n| \"Table_2\" | b79127cd6d99b9aa382e3de82802bc628a8382e62223ecbe883bc3c5d29bd4c7 | missing |\n| \"Table_3\" | ecddbace22768b5793d4a2f0eee8ff62abc53eaa3228246a85e91981798a65f5 | missing |\n| \"Table_4\" | e31ec37123a54c60a2c8aad4b33da572252d8cc90bc502665ff82faefb78c10b | missing |\n\nRelated workbooks:\n- None\n\nWork through every sheet listed above using the skill's workflow. Use\n`codemode` scripts to call the recipe tools, and batch the work: for example,\nlist the workbook and check templates for all sheets in one script, then read\ngrids and test recipes a few sheets at a time. Keep script output short.\n\nName dimensions from `dictionary/dimensions.csv` (see the skill's\n`references/naming.md`); declare any name it lacks in `new_dimensions`.\n\nWrite each recipe to `tidy-recipes/<sheet_sha256>.json` and finish every sheet\nwith `submit_recipe`. You may only write recipe files for this workbook.\n\nEnd with one line per sheet: `sheet | kind | status | records | remaining failures`."
